# Editors
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Messages the file mailer writes in development, and the CVs the file store
# keeps. Correspondence and documents belonging to people outside this firm, and
# not something to commit.
#
# Anchored to where they are actually written: beside the application's content
# root when it is run from the repository, and at the root of a published tree.
# These rules used to read "mail/" and "cvs/", which git matches at any depth —
# so they also matched src/JiranisokoTech.Application/Mail,
# src/JiranisokoTech.Infrastructure/Mail and tests/JiranisokoTech.Tests/Mail,
# and the entire mail module was silently unaddable. Nothing complained,
# because the files were on the disk of the machine they were written on.
/mail/
/cvs/
src/JiranisokoTech.Web/mail/
src/JiranisokoTech.Web/cvs/

# Worktrees the agent tooling creates. Not part of the project.
.claude/worktrees/
